Actually turn HTTPS-First Balanced Mode on by default.

aerium-https-first-balanced.patch already sets the registered default of
prefs::kHttpsFirstBalancedMode to true, but that alone does nothing, and
"Always use secure connections" still reads off on a fresh profile.

The reason is in IsBalancedModeEnabled() in
chrome/browser/ssl/https_upgrades_util.cc:

  bool user_has_modified_settings =
      prefs->HasPrefPath(prefs::kHttpsOnlyModeEnabled) ||
      prefs->HasPrefPath(prefs::kHttpsFirstBalancedMode);
  if (!user_has_modified_settings) {
    ... return base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(
        features::kHttpsFirstBalancedModeAutoEnable);
  }
  return prefs->GetBoolean(prefs::kHttpsFirstBalancedMode);

HasPrefPath() is true only for a value the user has actually written, not
for one that merely has a non-default registered default. So on a fresh
profile the pref branch is never reached: the decision falls to
kHttpsFirstBalancedModeAutoEnable, which upstream ships disabled. The pref
reads true in chrome://prefs-internals while the feature stays off, which
is exactly the mismatch that was reported.

kHttpsFirstBalancedMode itself is already FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT, so
the balanced mode is available - it just is not being switched on for
anyone who has not visited the setting. Flipping the auto-enable feature
does that, and does not take the choice away: once the user toggles the
setting themselves, HasPrefPath() becomes true and their value wins.

Balanced rather than strict is deliberate. Strict mode
(kHttpsOnlyModeEnabled) also warns on private and local hosts - router
admin pages, localhost, NAS boxes, printers, intranet names - which cannot
hold a publicly trusted certificate and so become interstitials on every
visit. Balanced upgrades and warns on public sites only.

--- a/chrome/common/chrome_features.cc
+++ b/chrome/common/chrome_features.cc
@@ -1200,7 +1200,7 @@
 // Automatically enables HTTPS-First Mode in a balanced configuration when
 // possible.
 BASE_FEATURE(kHttpsFirstBalancedModeAutoEnable,
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // Kill switch for crbug.com/40892208.
 BASE_FEATURE(kHttpsFirstModeForAdvancedProtectionUsers,
